## 5. Smart AI & Automation Specifications

### 5.1 Trust Score Engine (Hybrid Rule-Based)
Worker Trust Score \( T \in [0, 100] \) is dynamically computed upon every job completion:

$$T = (R \times 40) + (C \times 25) + (V \times 15) + (S \times 10) + (P \times 10)$$

Where:
* \( R \): Normalized Average Customer Rating (\( \text{Rating} / 5 \)) [Weight: 40%]
* \( C \): Job Completion Rate (\( \text{Completed Jobs} / \text{Accepted Jobs} \)) [Weight: 25%]
* \( V \): Cooperative Document Verification Level (0 or 1) [Weight: 15%]
* \( S \): Safety & Complaint Record (\( 1 - (\text{Complaints} / \text{Total Jobs}) \)) [Weight: 10%]
* \( P \): Punctuality / On-Time Arrival Ratio [Weight: 10%]

### 5.2 AI Worker Recommendation Engine
Calculates a **Match Score** \( M_w \) for candidate workers within range:

$$M_w = 0.35 \times \text{TrustScore}_w + 0.35 \times \left(1 - \frac{\text{Distance}}{5\text{km}}\right) + 0.20 \times \text{SkillMatch} + 0.10 \times \text{PastJobsCount}$$

### 5.3 Demand Forecasting Engine (MVP)
* Uses synthetic historical booking data (12 months of simulated hourly/daily booking patterns across zip codes).
* Applies time-series forecasting (moving average + day-of-week seasonality coefficients) via a lightweight Node.js/Python endpoint to generate upcoming 7-day category demand metrics.

### 5.4 Sentiment Analysis Engine (Lightweight NLP)
* Processes customer review text using keyword lexicon & sentiment scoring (AFINN / VADER algorithm equivalent).
* Categorizes reviews into `POSITIVE`, `NEUTRAL`, `NEGATIVE`.
* Negative reviews automatically lower worker trust score slightly and raise an alert on the Admin Dashboard for dispute resolution.

